    <item>
      description : "1.337 OL08-00-040200"
      info        : "The root account must be the only account having unrestricted access to the OL 8 system.

GROUP ID: V-248874RULE ID: SV-248874r991589

If an account other than root also has a User Identifier (UID) of \"0\", it has root authority, giving that account unrestricted access to the entire operating system. Multiple accounts with a UID of \"0\" afford an opportunity for potential intruders to guess a password for a privileged account."
      solution    : "Change the UID of any account on the system, other than root, that has a UID of \"0\".

If the account is associated with system commands or applications, change the UID to one greater than \"0\" but less than \"1000\". Otherwise, assign a UID of greater than \"1000\" that has not already been assigned."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|I,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|1M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-248874r991589_rule,STIG-ID|OL08-00-040200,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-248874"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23791"
      name        : "passwd_zero_uid"
    </item>

